/**
@page tutorials Tutorials

Nane is designed so that the numerical objects used in code remain close to
the mathematics they represent. These tutorials focus on practical use of the
library rather than listing individual API members.

## First steps

- @ref getting_started "Getting Started" — add Nane to a small C++23 project and solve a first problem.
- @ref cmake_integration "Using Nane with CMake" — submodules, static builds, targets, and recommended project layout.

## Numerical tutorials

- @ref ode_tutorial "Solving ODEs" — formulate an IVP and solve a nonlinear pendulum.
- @ref calculus_tutorial "Numerical Calculus" — differentiation with stencils and integration with quadrature rules.
- @ref custom_methods "Defining Custom Numerical Methods" — provide your own Butcher tables, stencils, and quadrature rules.

## API reference

Tutorials explain workflows and mathematical intent. For individual classes,
functions, parameters, and return types, use the [API Reference](topics.html).
*/
